+    ) -> Union[torch.Tensor, None]:
+        """Build a mean 1.0 spatial loss weight that concentrates on target edges.
+
+        A latent space loss is nearly indifferent to a wide, low amplitude ramp
+        at an object boundary. That is the failure this fixes: instead of a hard
+        edge the model learns a soft semi transparent stroke around the subject,
+        because spreading a small error over a band of latent cells costs it
+        almost nothing. Here the boundary of the target image is located in pixel
+        space, max pooled down to the loss resolution, then dilated outward so
+        the band the halo occupies is weighted along with the edge itself.
